  "articleBody": "Expanding your kitchen changes how your entire home functions, but jumping in before planning the scope can lead to major budget surprises. When you add square footage or push out walls, you are dealing with structural framing, sub-trades, and local building approvals across Colorado communities.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice:\n- Wall structure: Taking down a load-bearing partition requires structural headers and proper support calculations before framing begins.\n- Utility rerouting: Moving your sink, dishwasher, or gas range means running new drain lines, gas piping, and dedicated electrical circuits.\n- Permit scope: Pushing beyond your original footprint triggers zoning reviews, structural plan checks, and trade permits.\n- Cabinet lead times: Finalizing your cabinet selections and field measurements early prevents costly delays between rough framing and trim work.\n\nWhen your remodel alters the building envelope or calls for mechanical changes, working with an experienced team ensures everything passes inspection smoothly. Abraham Becerra and the crew at HH Remodeling LLC coordinate framing, drywall, and finish carpentry while managing licensed plumbing and electrical sub-trades. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your kitchen addition plans.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
